animal crossing New Horizons is the game  that keeps on giving and that means we  have a handful of extra tips just for  you let's get to it  the ladder if you've been playing Animal  Crossing for a couple days now you might  be wondering how you climb up cliffs in  order to do that you'll need the  collapsible ladder which Tom Nook will  give you once you meet a few conditions  you'll need to pay off your first loan  to Tom Nook and upgrade to a house which  will then allow you to build nook's  cranny on the de nooks cranny opens Tom  Nook will give you access to the ladder  or you could just have a friend give one  to you  rocks regenerate don't like where a rock  is no problem  eat a piece of fruit and smash it with  your shovel the next day a new rock will  respond somewhere else on your island  just make sure you mind the rock of its  resources before you break it how to add  best friends when you visit a friends  island or a friend visits you over the  internet you can add them as a best  friend to do that open your Nook phone  scroll over to the best friends app and  you should be able to send a friend  request from there the benefits to  registering a friend as a best friend is  that you can use all your tools on their  Island you can send gifts and letters  and you can send messages to each other  with your Nook phone fishing tips if  you're a completionist you might have  your sights set on the cast master  challenge that requires you to catch a  hundred fish in a row it may seem  daunting but we have an odd tip that  could help you out if you are struggling  to catch fish we recommend plugging in  headphones and using your hearing to  catch a fish instead when you cast your  line in a fish nibbles close your eyes  when the fish finally bites you'll hear  a plunk press a right away to reel in  the fish this may not work for everyone  but it has helped a few of us complete  that challenge how to move your house  and other buildings unhappy with where  you built your Museum no problem once  you've unlocked the residence services  building you can move your house your  villagers houses and other key buildings  by talking to Tom Nook about  infrastructure keep in mind that you can  only move one building per day and it  can be pricey  how amiibo work amiibo and amiibo cards  have a couple of functions and Animal  Crossing new horizons first once you've  unlocked harves island you can scan your  amiibo and have characters pose for  pictures second once you unlock the  campsite and your first camper has moved  in you'll unlock the ability to scan and  villagers at the Nook stop machine using  amiibo they will show up on your island  instantaneously but you aren't  guaranteed to get them to move in right  away how to get the able sisters one of  the random visitors who can come to your  Island is Mabel a hedgehog who sells  clothes she's hoping to set up a store  but needs to establish some customers  first and that's where you come in buy a  bunch of her stuff and pretty soon  she'll ask to set up shop  unlike nook's cranny you don't have to  supply any materials talk to sable  everyday Mabel and her sister sable  operate the able sisters tailor shop  sable is the quieter one in the back and  at first she won't have much to say to  you but as you talk to her every single  day she'll eventually open up and even  give you gifts how to unlock Island  terraforming if you watch the Nintendo  Direct you might be wondering how and  when you get the island designer app  that lets you terraform and further  customize your island I don't want to  spoil too much here but basically you  have to roll credits this means that you  should continue to help out Tom Nook  until he achieves his personal dream  after you've done that he'll swing by  your house and give you the island  designer app right from the get-go  you'll be able to start building paths  but if you want to terraform your island  you'll need to use your nook miles at  the nuke stop machine to unlock permits  for both water scaping and cliff  building if there's anything we missed  please let us know in the comments below  and be sure to check out our other tips  videos here on YouTube or gamespot.com  thank you so much for watching  [Music]
 

